config TCA_FAS
	bool "TCA kernel-side Frame Aware Scheduling (FAS)"
	depends on TRACEPOINTS && CPU_FREQ
	default n
	help
	  In-kernel Frame Aware Scheduling.  Hooks the in-tree
	  drm_vblank_event tracepoint, keeps an EMA of the vblank
	  interval and drives a FREQ_QOS_MIN request per CPU cluster
	  so the frame budget (1e9 / target_fps) is met.  This is the
	  same idea as the userspace fas-rs, but it needs no eBPF ring
	  buffer / BTF, so it works on 5.4.

	  Default off.  Knobs at /sys/kernel/tca_fas/.
